Chapter: DhcpAcquireE1000
  cites Net chapter DhcpIO
  cites Net chapter NetDriver
  cites Net chapter NetworkConfig

 The same acquisition over the Intel card rather than the NE2000, which
 is the card the demo runs on. The two arms differ only in their
 `.vmargs`, so a difference in the rows is a difference in the card and
 nothing else.

 The card row is what makes this arm distinguishable from its sibling: if
 `net-driver-bring-up` failed to bind, the seam falls back to the NE2000
 and prints so, and with `-e1000-nat` set that fallback has no wire at
 all -- the NAT is on the Intel part. So a run that says ne2000 here has
 not tested what this file is named for.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    let card = net-driver-bring-up
    in let mac = net-driver-mac
    in act
      cfg <- dhcp-io-configure mac "codex" 305419896 200000 0
      print-line-uni ("card   : " & net-driver-card-name card)
      print-line-uni ("config : " & format-net-config cfg)
      print-line-uni ("leased : " & (if net-is-configured cfg then "yes" else "no"))
    end
  end

